<!--
    A frame local in the outgoing-argument area does not anchor a run of
    forwarded registers.

        d3: push %rbx; mov %rsi,%rbx; lea msg(%rip),%rdi; sub $0x30,%rsp
            movq $f1,(%rsp); movq $f2,0x8(%rsp); movq $f3,0x10(%rsp)
            movq $f4,0x18(%rsp); xor %eax,%eax; call xprintf
            movdqa (%rsp),%xmm0; movdqa 0x10(%rsp),%xmm1
            xor %edx,%edx; xor %ecx,%ecx; xor %r8d,%r8d; xor %r9d,%r9d
            call take; add $0x30,%rsp; pop %rbx; ret

    is the shape of mirai's `main` (decbench O2): six function pointers
    stored at [rsp] before the first call, `xprintf("DEBUG MODE YO\n")`, and
    reloaded after it.  rsi..r9 are the function's own incoming registers,
    untouched at the call, so `passthrough`'s chain rule
    (kuna-passthrough-fwdchain.xml) kept them out of the inactive run, and the
    active stack slots behind them anchored it: the call printed
    `xprintf(msg,a1,a2,a3,a4,a5,f1,f2,f3,f4)` and d3 gained five parameters.
    With every argument register in front of it forwarded, a stack slot holding
    a constant the function stored is a local, not an argument the forwarded
    registers lead up to (kuna_passthrough.rs, ends_rescued_run); where the
    reload is already linked to the slot, as in mirai, survives_call says so
    as well.  `xprintf` saves rsi..r9 for its va_list and `take` is outside
    the image.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 "active-input-trial-scoring", option `passthrough`.
    Both passes print the option-off call.
-->
